The Nautilus DevOps team is setting up monitoring in their AWS account. As part of this, they need to create a CloudWatch alarm.

Using Terraform, perform the following:

Task Details:
Create a CloudWatch alarm named nautilus-alarm.
The alarm should monitor CPU utilization of an EC2 instance.
Trigger the alarm when CPU utilization exceeds 80%.
Set the evaluation period to 5 minutes.
Use a single evaluation period.
Ensure that the entire configuration is implemented using Terraform. The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. 
Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
To create the CloudWatch alarm, you will need to reference the EC2 instance. Since the task doesn't provide an instance ID, you'll need to look it up using a data source, then configure the alarm with the specified metrics.

Here is the content for your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf file:

hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

# Look up the existing EC2 instance (adjust the filter if your instance has a specific Name tag)
data "aws_instance" "target_instance" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Name"
    values = ["*"] # Replace with the actual Name tag if known, e.g., "nautilus-ec2"
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "nautilus_alarm" {
  alarm_name          = "nautilus-alarm"
  comparison_operator = "GreaterThanThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 1
  metric_name         = "CPUUtilization"
  namespace           = "AWS/EC2"
  period              = 300
  statistic           = "Average"
  threshold           = 80
  alarm_description   = "Alarm when CPU utilization exceeds 80%"

  dimensions = {
    InstanceId = data.aws_instance.target_instance.id
  }
}
💡 Key Details
Finding the Instance: Since no instance ID is given, the data "aws_instance" block uses a filter to locate it. If the instance has a specific Name tag, replace "*" with that value. If your environment only has one instance, the filter might still work, but it's safer to specify the tag .

Alarm Configuration: The alarm is set to trigger when CPUUtilization is GreaterThanThreshold 80% for 1 evaluation period of 300 seconds (5 minutes) .

Namespace: For EC2 metrics, the namespace must be AWS/EC2 .

🚀 Execution Steps
Run the following in the terminal inside /home/bob/terraform:

bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
