Given that you're using LocalStack (the http://aws:4566 endpoints), you need to work with the resources available in your LocalStack environment. Since no EC2 instance ID is provided, you'll need to create an EC2 instance first (or look up an existing one) and then attach the alarm to it.

Here is the main.tf that creates the EC2 instance and the CloudWatch alarm:

hcl
# Create an EC2 instance to monitor
resource "aws_instance" "nautilus_instance" {
  ami           = "ami-0c101f26f147fa7fd"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = "nautilus-ec2"
  }
}

# Create the CloudWatch alarm for CPU utilization
resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "nautilus_alarm" {
  alarm_name          = "nautilus-alarm"
  comparison_operator = "GreaterThanThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 1
  metric_name         = "CPUUtilization"
  namespace           = "AWS/EC2"
  period              = 300
  statistic           = "Average"
  threshold           = 80
  alarm_description   = "Alarm when CPU utilization exceeds 80%"

  dimensions = {
    InstanceId = aws_instance.nautilus_instance.id
  }
}
💡 Key Details
EC2 Instance: Since LocalStack doesn't have pre-existing instances, we create one to attach the alarm to. The AMI ami-0c101f26f147fa7fd is a common Amazon Linux 2 AMI used in KodeKloud labs .

Alarm Name: nautilus-alarm as required.

Metric: CPUUtilization from the AWS/EC2 namespace.

Threshold: 80 with GreaterThanThreshold.

Evaluation Periods: 1 (single evaluation period).

Period: 300 seconds (5 minutes).

Dimension: Ties the alarm to the specific EC2 instance.

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
⚠️ If an EC2 Instance Already Exists
If the environment already has an instance and you're not supposed to create one, replace the aws_instance resource with a data block:

hcl
data "aws_instance" "existing" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Name"
    values = ["nautilus-ec2"] # adjust to match the actual tag
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "nautilus_alarm" {
  alarm_name          = "nautilus-alarm"
  comparison_operator = "GreaterThanThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 1
  metric_name         = "CPUUtilization"
  namespace           = "AWS/EC2"
  period              = 300
  statistic           = "Average"
  threshold           = 80
  alarm_description   = "Alarm when CPU utilization exceeds 80%"

  dimensions = {
    InstanceId = data.aws_instance.existing.id
  }
}
